{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "engine",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "sad_engine — one fixed-alignment lane (IMPLEMENTED wrapper)",
      "x": 2160,
      "y": -60,
      "width": 1180,
      "height": 650,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "legend",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Module blocks · signals and status\n\n**Green** = implemented RTL module. **Orange** = proposed interconnect / controller, NOT RTL.\n**Purple** = shared input/control. **Cyan** = reasoning next to the datapath.\n\nRead left → right. The green sad_engine outline CONTAINS its two RTL submodules; the orange bank would replicate that whole outline. Arrows are signals or explicitly labelled conceptual replication, not software calls.",
      "x": -60,
      "y": -590,
      "width": 850,
      "height": 350,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "input",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## paired rectified raster streams\n\n**IN** synchronized left_pixel, right_pixel; accepted-pixel valid; frame start/clear.\n**OUT** left/right pixel stream at the same (x,y).\n\nExternal producer / Nios V path: NOT wired in RTL. Pause both streams together at each completed output row; no ready pin exists on the current blocks. Rectification happens upstream.",
      "x": -60,
      "y": 140,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 410,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "controls",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## clock, reset and frame boundary\n\n**clk, rst_n** to implemented RTL. Reset is synchronous active-low.\n**frame_clear** to BOTH row buffers at new frame; it also invalidates planned downstream state.\n**row_clear** to cache + every engine ONLY between completed window rows, after the final score is consumed. Never clear the row buffers at each output row: they must retain K-row history.",
      "x": 820,
      "y": -590,
      "width": 590,
      "height": 370,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "rowL",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## circular_row_buffer · LEFT (implemented module, proposed second-instance wiring)\n\n**IN** clk, rst_n, clear_i = frame_clear, valid_i, pixel_i[PIXEL_W]\n**OUT** valid_o, column_o[K×PIXEL_W] = L[x], row_last_o\n\nK image rows, same x. Registered vertical column; oldest row in low slice. One accepted pixel at a time. This is NOT a disparity cache.",
      "x": 500,
      "y": -30,
      "width": 450,
      "height": 400,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "rowR",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## circular_row_buffer · RIGHT (same RTL, second proposed instance)\n\n**IN** clk, rst_n, clear_i = frame_clear, valid_i, pixel_i[PIXEL_W]\n**OUT** valid_o, column_o[K×PIXEL_W] = R[x], row_last_o\n\nSame accepted-pixel schedule as LEFT; synchronized x and y required. Registered one-image vertical column. No shift-by-d in this module.",
      "x": 500,
      "y": 560,
      "width": 450,
      "height": 390,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "left-delay",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## left column + tag delay (PLANNED)\n\n**IN** L[x], valid, row_last, x / row identity\n**OUT** registered L[x] and matching valid + coordinates\n\nExactly one register stage, matching the proposed right cache shift edge. Left and tapped right must reach a lane for the SAME x on the SAME edge.",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": -30,
      "width": 490,
      "height": 370,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "cache",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## right-column shift cache (PLANNED)\n\n**IN** R[x][K×PIXEL_W], valid, row_last, x / row identity, row_clear\n**OUT** Q[0..31] columns + per-tap valid/coordinate\n\nOn each valid *complete* row-buffer column: Q[0]←R[x], Q[d]←old Q[d−1]. Thus Q[d]=R[x−d]. Hold on bubbles. Invalidate at output-row boundary; never shift warmup-row garbage. Registers store whole COLUMNS, not pixels or column SAD costs.",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 550,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 510,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "align",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 32 fixed disparity taps (PLANNED wiring)\n\n**IN** Q[0..31], valid + x, delayed L[x]\n**OUT per d** aligned pair (L[x], R[x−d]), accepted-valid, disparity tag d\n\nTap d is just a selected cache position / wire to lane d; no 32-cycle serial search. d=0 uses Q[0]. d=31 uses Q[31]. A tap is NOT another image-row ring or a multiplier.",
      "x": 1670,
      "y": 490,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 450,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "controller",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## row/metadata controller (PLANNED)\n\n**IN** synchronized row_last_o, row-buffer valid, x/row tags; output-valid drain status\n**OUT** paired input pause, row_clear for cache + ALL engines, metadata/masks toward comparator\n\nAt row end, pause the pixel producer, let final R[x] enter cache and engines, drain engine outputs, then clear on a separate edge. Restart next row afterward. Row buffers keep their vertical history.",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": -600,
      "width": 570,
      "height": 450,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "colsad",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## column_sad · inside sad_engine (IMPLEMENTED)\n\n**IN** clk, rst_n, clear_i, valid_i, left_column_i[K×PIXEL_W], right_column_i[K×PIXEL_W]\n**OUT** column_sum_o[COL_W], valid_o\n\nK parallel |L−R| leaves, registered balanced adder tree. For K=11: accepts one aligned pair/edge; column result is registered at edge t+4.",
      "x": 2210,
      "y": 90,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 420,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "colbuf",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## column_sum_buffer · inside sad_engine (IMPLEMENTED)\n\n**IN** clk, rst_n, clear_i, valid_i, column_sum_i[COL_W]\n**OUT** sad_o[SAD_W], valid_o\n\nCircular history of K−1 previous column COSTS. Computes horizontal K-column SAD = history_sum + newest cost and registers it. NOT the right-column pixel cache.",
      "x": 2760,
      "y": 90,
      "width": 510,
      "height": 420,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "bank",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## replicate the ENTIRE boxed sad_engine (PLANNED)\n\n**d=0, 1, …, 31:** one instance of the GREEN wrapper per disparity. Each lane owns BOTH its column_sad and column_sum_buffer state.\n**IN lane d** delayed L[x], Q[d]=R[x−d], per-lane accepted-valid, row_clear.\n**OUT lane d** (sad_o, valid_o, d, delayed coordinate). Only ONE standalone engine RTL exists today; no 32-lane wrapper or fan-out is implemented.",
      "x": 2160,
      "y": 680,
      "width": 1180,
      "height": 350,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "winner",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## minimum (SAD, disparity) comparator (PLANNED)\n\n**IN** 32 matched-coordinate SAD scores, lane valid bits, disparity IDs\n**OUT** valid best disparity and cost; tie policy: lower d\n\nInvalid right-border/window lanes cannot win. Either compare only the common interior x≥K−1+31, or mask unavailable lanes individually and carry coordinate tags through pipeline. Metric depth is downstream, not this block.",
      "x": 3550,
      "y": 115,
      "width": 530,
      "height": 460,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "why-cache",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Why a column cache and where the taps sit\n\nA row buffer turns serial pixels into a VERTICAL K-pixel column at x. Stereo disparity is a HORIZONTAL offset between columns, so shift complete right columns AFTER the right row buffer.\n\n```text\nrow-buffer output       L[x]                  R[x]\n                           │                    │\nnext clock            delay L[x]    Q0←R[x], Q1←old Q0, ...\n                           │                    │\nengine d inputs       L[x]              Q[d]=R[x−d]\n```\nExample x=6, d=2: lane 2 compares L[6] with R[4] for all K vertical pixel pairs. Both operands have the SAME row-window endpoint y. The horizontal K-column history lives INSIDE lane 2’s column_sum_buffer.",
      "x": 550,
      "y": 1210,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 610,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "border",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Validity, latency and row boundaries · planned contract\n\n**Per-lane input:** suppress engine d until its tap exists (x≥d). With K consecutive accepted aligned columns, the first complete right window ends at x=d+K−1. For a simultaneous 32-way minimum, compare only x≥K−1+31, OR mask invalid lanes correctly. Do not pad missing right pixels with zeros and score them.\n\n**Edge timing:** row buffers register L[x]/R[x] at edge t; cache and left delay register them at t+1; sad_engine samples matched operands at t+2. A K=11 engine outputs its completed-window score after t+7 (provided it has K accepted columns); comparator adds its own planned latency.\n\n**End of output row:** the final pixel reaches row buffers at t, cache at t+1, engine at t+2; consume final score at t+7, then clear cache and engine on a separate edge. Pause upstream pixels while draining; clearing both row buffers here destroys vertical history. Reset cache/tag validity at new frame too.\n\n**Status:** timing above is an architectural proposal for the not-yet-coded cache/controller/bank, NOT verified top-level RTL.",
      "x": 1900,
      "y": 1210,
      "width": 1440,
      "height": 720,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "row-source",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "Circular Row Buffer.md",
